{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Converting a Throwing Expression to a Result","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)-62kyq"],"anchor":"Converting-a-Throwing-Expression-to-a-Result"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/preserving-the-results-of-a-throwing-expression","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Call the initializer that wraps a throwing expression when you need to serialize","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or memoize the result.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sometimes you need to preserve the entire result of a function call or other expression","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that can either throw or return a value. For example, you may need to serialize the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"result or pass it as a value to another part of your app that handles the result","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"data. Use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result","isActive":true},{"text":" type in these scenarios to capture the result of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"potentially failing operation.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Identify a Throwing Expression to Preserve","anchor":"Identify-a-Throwing-Expression-to-Preserve","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Typically, you use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do-catch"},{"text":" statements to handle throwing expressions immediately,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"but sometimes you need to store the whole result of the operation for later processing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"during tasks like analyzing a batch of calls. The following example introduces an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API that generates random numbers, but that fails approximately half of the time."}]},{"code":["enum EntropyError: Error {","    case entropyDepleted","}","","struct UnreliableRandomGenerator {","    func random() throws -> Int {","        if Bool.random() {","            return Int.random(in: 1...100)","        } else {","            throw EntropyError.entropyDepleted","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Convert the Throwing Expression to a Result","anchor":"Convert-the-Throwing-Expression-to-a-Result","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You preserve the return value or thrown error from a throwing expression using the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"},{"type":"text","text":" enumeration’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)-62kyq"},{"type":"text","text":" initializer. Invoke"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the throwing expression inside the closure you pass to the initializer:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let singleSample = Result { try UnreliableRandomGenerator().random() }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In most scenarios, you use the preserved result as part of broader functionality","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"in your code. For example, you may run a series of randomness tests and compute the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"statistical average of both a range of numbers returned from a random number generator,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"as well as the failure rate of calling the API. In these cases, you need to store","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the whole result rather than just the success value or that the API call failed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example uses the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)-62kyq","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" initializer in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"broader context of saving a series of calls for later statistical analysis:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct RandomnessMonitor {","    let randomnessSource: UnreliableRandomGenerator","    var results: [Result<Int, Error>] = []","","    init(generator: UnreliableRandomGenerator) {","        randomnessSource = generator","    }","","    mutating func sample() {","        let sample = Result { try randomnessSource.random() }","        results.append(sample)","    }","","    func summary() -> (Double, Double) {","        let totals = results.reduce((sum: 0, count: 0)) { total, sample in","            switch sample {","            case .success(let number):","                return (total.sum + number, total.count)","            case .failure:","                return (total.sum, total.count + 1)","            }","        }","","        return (","            average: Double(totals.sum) \/ Double(results.count - totals.count),","            failureRate: Double(totals.count) \/ Double(results.count)","        )","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Running the analysis on a sufficiently large sample generates an average number near"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"50 and a failure rate near 50%:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var monitor = RandomnessMonitor(generator: UnreliableRandomGenerator())","(0..<1000).forEach { _ in monitor.sample() }","let (average, failureRate) = monitor.summary()","print(\"Average value: \\(average), failure rate: \\(failureRate * 100.0)%.\")","\/\/ Prints values such as: \"Average value: 47.95, failure rate: 48.69%.\""]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/preserving-the-results-of-a-throwing-expression"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"title":"Preserving the Results of a Throwing Expression","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Result":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/result","title":"Result","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Result"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A value that represents either a success or a failure, including an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"associated value in each case.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Result","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/numbers-and-basic-values":{"abstract":[{"text":"Model data with numbers, Boolean values, and other fundamental types.","type":"text"}],"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","title":"Numbers and Basic Values","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","type":"topic"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift","type":"topic","title":"Standard Library","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Standard Library","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the essential types provided by Swift’s standard librar